# @corpus current
# law.projection.one / law.paren.one / law.projection.head — one projection algebra;
# relation projection is not curry.
#
# Declaration: `to(str) = (value)` → relation to, projection str, subject value.
# Invocation ladder (shortest unique form): value:to(str) → value
# when graph proves each step (INFER-ONE). value:to() is not a canonical rung.
#
# THE FILE NAMED FOR THE PROJECTION ALGEBRA STOPPED CARRYING IT. Commit
# 98ceb52c — an argument-projection migration whose message never mentions
# projection heads — rewrote `to(str) = (value)` into `to__str = (value)` and
# `read(i64) = (lx, b)` into `read__i64 = (lx, b)`. THE ORACLE LINE DID NOT
# MOVE, and it could not have: `17` is answered by the BUILT-IN conversion and
# never reached either declaration. Measured — a user `to(str)` whose body
# answers `value + 900` still prints 17 — so this file's number is IDENTICAL
# whether the levelled declaration is present, mangled, or deleted outright.
# `idol fmt` performs the same rewrite today, which is why the mangled spelling
# is its FIXPOINT: the formatter's normal form is the loss.
#
# THE `to` ROW IS KEPT because the conversion ladder is this file's first law,
# but it proves nothing about the projection HEAD and never did. The `lift` and
# `cast` rows are what reach a declaration. `lift` is levelled; `cast` is the
# same two edges in the mangled spelling 98ceb52c and `idol fmt` rewrite them
# into, and the oracle requires the two families to AGREE cell for cell over
# identical operands. They are ONE identity and not two: declared at the same
# key they collide as `lift__str` — "ambiguous call to overloaded function" —
# which gate/projection.sh runs rather than asserts. `cast` is the retired form
# kept as a witness; it is not a second face to migrate onto.
#
# TWO EDGES MUST DISAGREE, so a single-edge implementation that kept the last
# declaration prints one number twice. `str` and `i64` are concrete descriptors
# in the projection head — the point `read(i64)` carried before it was mangled,
# and never an adjective protocol.
#
# THE PARAMETER IS TYPED AND THE INVOCATION IS OPERATION-FIRST, and neither is
# a preference. The header's own untyped `to(str) = (value)` refuses at
# `parameter-type-unsupported:to__str` — the compiler spelling the MANGLED name
# for the levelled face, which is the identity restated by the realizer. The
# canonical subject-first call `n:lift(str)` refuses at
# `missing-application-id`, so `lift(str)(n)` — the form CLAUDE.md calls
# migratable debt — is the only spelling of this edge that runs. The retired
# `to__str = (value)` and `read__i64 = (lx, b)` bodies are gone from here
# because they refuse and the number never reached them; gate/projection.sh
# runs all three as probes. They are owed, not worked around.
# expect: 17 917 107 917 107

lift(str) = (value: i64): i64
  value + 900

lift(i64) = (value: i64): i64
  value + 90

cast__str: i64 = (value: i64)
  value + 900

cast__i64: i64 = (value: i64)
  value + 90

n: i64 = 17
a = lift(str)(n)
b = lift(i64)(n)
c = cast__str(n)
d = cast__i64(n)
print(n:to(str))
print("{a} {b} {c} {d}")
0
